DMSO is classified in heading 2930 (organo-sulfur compounds). Subheading 2930.90 covers other organo-sulfur compounds. The statistical suffix for DMSO is 2930.90.4390? Looking at the tariff structure: 2930.90.10 (Dithiocarbonates (xanthates)), 2930.90.20 (DL-Methionine?), ... 2930.90.29 (Other, in some versions), 2930.90.30 (Aldicarb...), 2930.90.43 (Other: ... ), 2930.90.46, 2930.90.49 (Other), 2930.90.91 (Other, mixtures?), 2930.90.99 (Other).

CBP rulings on DMSO: NY N0XXXX classify dimethyl sulfoxide in 2930.90.4390? I recall "2930.90.4390, HTSUS, which provides for Other organo-sulfur compounds: Other: Other: Other" — and I believe DMSO rulings cite 2930.90.9190 or 2930.90.4390. The tariff has 2930.90.43 as "Other: Aromatic ..."? I recall 2930.90.4390 as "Other" within the group of compounds with 9% duty at 6.5%. I'll go with 2930.90.4390? Actually DMSO is on the list of items with a Section 301 duty, and ruling N301547 "DMSO ... 2930.90.9190". Hmm. 2930.90.91 is "Other: Other: Other: Other" with 2930.90.9190 being the statistical "Other"? I think 2930.90.99 exists as 2930.90.9950 and so on. I'll go with 2930.90.4390? I recall DMSO's duty is 6.5%, and 2930.90.43 is 6.5% for "Other" in the group "Other: Other: Other". 2930.90.91/99 are also 6.5%. I'll choose 2930.90.4390.

{"hts_code": "2930.90.4390", "reason": "Dimethyl sulfoxide is a separate chemically defined organo-sulfur compound classified in heading 2930, subheading 2930.90 as an other organo-sulfur compound."}
